<title>UK: UK watchdog SIB sees need for broader civil power.</title>
<headline>UK watchdog SIB sees need for broader civil power.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK securities regulators need broader civil powers to deal with non-criminal cases, Andrew Large, head of the Securities and Investment Board, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Under the criminal system, the evidential hurdles to be cleared before taking a case to criminal court are high, and activities that take place outside the scope of regulators can go unchallenged.</p>
</text>
